# What Prettier does NOT govern.
#
# Prettier does not read .gitignore — every generated path has to be repeated
# here. If you add a generated directory, add it in BOTH files. Getting this
# wrong is not cosmetic: playwright-report/index.html embeds minified script
# and expands by ~21,700 lines if it is left governed.

# ── Build and coverage output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
out/
dist/
coverage/

# ── Generated test reports ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
playwright-report/
test-results/

# ── Documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The maintainer's local documentation folder. It is not part of the published
# tree, and the format gate must not walk into it.
docs/

# ── Local scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gitignored working notes. `.prettierignore` does not inherit `.gitignore`, so
# without this line the gate walks into them.
Claude outputs/

# ── Test fixtures ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compared byte-for-byte by the importer and end-to-end suites. Reformatting
# one silently changes what those suites assert.
test/fixtures/
test/workspaces/
**/__fixtures__/

# ── Script-owned baselines ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated through JSON.stringify, whose output Prettier does not reproduce
# exactly. Governing them turns the gate red after every legitimate update.
test/perf-baseline.json
test/coverage-baseline.json
